=== Summary ===
Artifact: shared-surfaces/HelpIcon — native Jetpack Compose + Material 3 parity port of
  web/src/components/ui/HelpIcon.tsx (the field-level "(?)" icon that reveals help copy via a tooltip).
Files: app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/HelpIcon/{HelpIcon.kt, HelpIconModel.kt}
       app/src/test/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/HelpIcon/HelpIconModelTest.kt
       app/src/androidTest/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/HelpIcon/HelpIconUiTest.kt
Package: io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.helpicon (hyphenated/PascalCase dir cannot be a Kotlin
  package — InvalidPackageDeclaration suppressed, as on every sibling surface).

States reproduced (exactly the branches the web source draws): HIDDEN when no help copy is supplied
  (web `if (!text) return null`) and SHOWN otherwise, crossed with the three accessible-name outcomes —
  an explicit override (web `ariaLabel`), the per-field "Help for {field}" (web `for` => t('a11y.helpFor')),
  or the generic "More info" (web t('help.tooltip.iconLabel')). The generic data-surface states
  (loading/empty/error/stale/offline) do NOT apply: the component fetches nothing and binds no hook (its
  only "data source", useTranslation, is the i18n facade, not a query). The web `side` placement prop is
  omitted as a documented platform adaptation — Material 3 anchors a tooltip adjacent to its trigger and
  resolves the side from available space (Android HIG); the sibling components/ui/HelpIcon + Tooltip atoms
  already omit it. Rationale documented in HelpIconModel.kt header (honesty covenant: no scope narrowing).

i18n (P1/S10): the two accessible-name strings resolve via R.string.translation_a11y_helpFor ("Help for
  %1$s") and R.string.translation_help_tooltip_iconLabel ("More info") — both already in the catalog, the
  exact keys the web source reads. No new catalog keys were added (the catalog is a P1/S10 dependency
  outside this artifact's allowed files).

Accessibility: the trigger's contentDescription is the resolved accessible name, so TalkBack announces
  "Help for {field}" (or "More info"); rendering is delegated to the shared components/ui/HelpIcon atom
  (Material 3 RichTooltip over a 48dp IconButton drawing TeslaGlyphs.Help), which reveals the copy on tap
  and auto-dismisses on an outside tap — the touch-idiomatic equivalent of the web hover/focus reveal +
  Escape-to-dismiss. The web `data-help-for` audit hook is mirrored as the trigger's testTag
  (help-icon-trigger[-{for}]). Font scale / light / dark / high-contrast handled by the atom + design tokens.

Telemetry (P1/S11): one-shot PII-safe view.opened{surface=HelpIcon} on first composition.

Tests:
  - HelpIconModelTest (off-device, the testReleaseUnitTest gate): 14 tests, 0 failures — help-text
    resolution (text ?? content), the render-nothing gate (Hidden vs Shown), accessible-name selection
    with override > per-field > generic precedence, the data-help-for testTag, and the view.opened
    diagnostic (adapter/projection + a11y-label coverage).
  - HelpIconUiTest (androidTest): per-state Compose UI + a11y assertions (per-field label / generic label /
    explicit override / hidden-when-no-copy). connectedAndroidTest needs a device/emulator (not on this
    runner); the offline testReleaseUnitTest gate covers the pure model. ktlint did lint the androidTest
    source set (green). The UiTest calls assertDoesNotExist as a SemanticsNodeInteraction member (no bad
    import), matching the passing FormFieldUiTest sibling.

Capability: Jetpack Compose (BOM 2026.04.01) + Material 3 + Kotlin 2.4.0 present — capability satisfied
  (the prompt's "Kotlin 2.2.x" predates the ADR-012 locked 2.4.0 baseline). JDK 21, Android SDK present,
  Gradle 8.14.5. NOT blocked.

